  "text": "Here's the Python code that implements the desired behavior:\n\n```python\nimport string\n\ndef word_histogram(text):\n    # Create a dictionary to store word frequencies\n    word_freq = {}\n    \n    # Process the text\n    words = text.lower().split()\n    \n    # Remove punctuation\n    new_words = []\n    for word in words:\n        clean_word = ''\n        for char in word:\n            if char not in string.punctuation:\n                clean_word += char\n        if clean_word:  # Only add non-empty words\n            new_words.append(clean_word)\n    \n    # Count frequency of each word\n    for word in new_words:\n        word_freq[word] = word_freq.get(word, 0) + 1\n    \n    return word_freq\n```\n\nThis implementation:\n\n1. Converts all text to lowercase\n2. Splits the text into words\n3. Removes punctuation character by character from each word\n4. Only includes non-empty words\n5. Uses a dictionary to count frequency of each word",
